        "original_id": "253c1bfe-24bf-573c-ad40-b0d75613299b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Keith Scholey, Alastair Fothergill\n- Films: Bears, African Cats, Aliens of the Deep\n- Organizations: Disneynature, Walden Media, Walt Disney Pictures, BBC One, BBC Natural History Unit\n- TV Series: Big Cat Diary\n- Places: Alaska\n\nFacts:\n- In 1996, the first series of Big Cat Diary was broadcast on BBC One.\n- In 1996, Keith Scholey developed and jointly produced the first series of Big Cat Diary.\n- Keith Scholey later became Head of the BBC Natural History Unit.\n- Aliens of the Deep was produced by Walden Media and Walt Disney Pictures.\n- In 2014, Bears was released as a nature documentary film about a family of brown bears living in the coastal mountain ranges of Alaska.\n- Keith Scholey co-directed African Cats with Alastair Fothergill for Disneynature.\n- Keith Scholey co-directed Bears with Alastair Fothergill for Disneynature.",
